{"name":"Hush Pink","hex":"#f8e9e2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become quiet.","To make quiet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A silence, especially after some noise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hush"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hush (Billy Joe Royal song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Hush\" is a song written by American songwriter and pop musician Joe South, for singer Billy Joe Royal. The song was a #14 hit by Somebody's Image in 1967; Morris re-released a new recording with his band The Rubes in 1980. It was also recorded by Deep Purple in 1968, Blue Swede in 1975, and by Kula Shaker in 1997. These groups each had Hot 100 hits with their versions."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/84/Hush_%28Billy_Joe_Royal_song%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hush_(Billy_Joe_Royal_song)","wikidata":"Q2631389"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/be/Deeppurp